{title: The Carmelite}
{subtitle: 2 Samuel 23:35; 1 Chronicles 11:37; 2 Samuel 23:24–39; 23:8–9}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Gm7] | [C] |
| [Fmaj7] | [Bbmaj7] | [Gm7] | [A7sus4] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Among the [Dm]thirty [Am7/C]brave men [Bb]stood
A name re[Gm]corded [C]in the [Fmaj7]book
Hezro the [Bb]Carme[C]lite was [Dm]found
In [Bb]David's mig[Am]hty compa[Dm]ny
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
No spear or battle is [Am7/C]named for [Bb]him
No kill [Gm]is writ[C]ten in the [Fmaj7]text
He stands [Bb]among the [C]heroes [Dm]then
In the [Bb]list of [Am7]those who [Dm]served
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Chronicled a[C]gain we [Dm]see
The [Bb]same name [C]in the [F]scroll
Hezro the [Bb]Carme[C]lite ap[Dm]pears
In the [Bb]record [Am7]of the [Dm]bold
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]Part of the elite [C]group they [Dm]were
[Bb]Loyal to the [C]king of [F]old
[Bb]Serving in the [C]army [Dm]days
When the [Bb]kingdom grew [A]strong
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Hezro the Car[Dm]me[C]lite is [Bbmaj7]named
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
